#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-AD0419 expect=violation domain=ADSL
# Rule:Description: On a given record, TRxxPGyN is populated and TRxxPGy is not populated
#note "tr01pg1n populated, tr01pg1 empty, both spelled in lower case. Column names match case-insensitively on every surface (owner ruling 2026-09-28), so the lowercase spelling a SAS dataset may carry satisfies the Requirements.Variables.All templates and the rule executes with the same verdict as on the uppercase twin (CDISC-AD0419-invalid): CR419 — TRxxPGy is not populated where TRxxPGyN is (ADaMIG 1.3 Table 3.2.4, one-to-one mapping) -> violation."
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt row=1 USUBJID=01-701-1015
dataset ADSL class=ADSL
col STUDYID type=Char
col USUBJID type=Char
col tr01pg1n type=Char
col tr01pg1 type=Char
---
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1015 | VAL |
---
